reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-9-// Only the pieces needed so far: a dict VALUE (so `{}` inside a mixed list evaluates and
reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k:10:// `isinstance(x, int)` rejects it), the `{k: v, ...}` literal, and `.keys()`. More dict ops (subscript
reference-semantics/semantics/dict.k-11-// / `.get()` / `.values()` / dict `==`) are added as dict problems need them — kept minimal + additive.
